Pass the MSVC compile options to MSVC only.

On WIN32 the extension gets /O2 /EHsc /MD unconditionally. GCC and
Clang targeting MinGW-w64 read them as input file names and the build
stops. MinGW-w64 compilers need none of them: they use C++ exceptions
by default and link the C runtime the toolchain was built for.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -201,7 +201,9 @@
 
 
     # Ensure /MD and exception model are set
-    target_compile_options(_jpype PRIVATE /O2 /EHsc /MD)
+    if(MSVC)
+        target_compile_options(_jpype PRIVATE /O2 /EHsc /MD)
+    endif()
 else()
     # Additional libraries for non-Windows
     target_link_libraries(_jpype PRIVATE
